expect	error
build	refused	the return type of `opt_sugar` may not name a borrowing struct: `It?` names a `borrows struct` (`It`), and a borrowing struct holds a LENT PLACE, so its values live only inside their window — the extent is the `for` statement, which is what makes the borrow trackable without a lifetime. A type argument, an existential, a field, a parameter and a plain return each outlive the window, so none of them can name one — which is what makes a generic identity wrapper unwritable rather than caught
